---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What BU4 is, how it relates to JEENISo, and how the team works together.">
  <section class="container section">
    <SectionHeading numeral="04" eyebrow="About" title="About Business Unit 4" />
    <p class="lead">
      {site.fullName} is one of the business units inside {site.parentOrg}, {site.parentOrgFull}.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container section grid-2">
    <div>
      <h2>What BU4 is</h2>
      <p>
        BU4 brings together seven engineering students at ENISo across applied computer science,
        embedded telecommunications, automotive software and industrial electronics. As a business
        unit of JEENISo, the team takes part in the Junior Enterprise's collective challenges and
        works on its own technical projects.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Relationship with JEENISo</h2>
      <p>
        JEENISo is the Junior Enterprise of ENISo (École Nationale d'Ingénieurs de Sousse). Each
        BU4 member is also a JEENISo member, and the team's work - including this website -
        contributes to JEENISo's broader activities.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container section grid-2">
    <div>
      <h2>How the team works</h2>
      <p>
        Members come from different specialties and bring different technical strengths -
        embedded systems, electronics, programming and web development. The team's first shared
        project, this portfolio website, was built collaboratively: content, design and
        development split across several members.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Where we want to go</h2>
      <p>
        Individually, members are working toward internships, certifications and specializations
        in fields like ADAS, embedded AI, IoT and web development. As BU4, the team is still early
        in establishing its collective project track record - see the{' '}
        <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}projects/`}>Projects</a> page for what's been
        confirmed so far.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--fs-400);
    max-width: 65ch;
  }
  .grid-2 {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  .grid-2 h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-600);
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .grid-2 {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-5);
    }
  }
</style>
